#usda 1.0
(
    """
    This museum case demonstrates that a reference with no other opinions
    composes the same as its target when the target uses nested relocates
    and inherits.

    feathers.usda: /FeathersRig/RWing inherits the class /FeathersRig/SymWing.
    Under SymWing, Deform/Flight01Rig/Control/X inherits the sibling class
    Deform/Flight01Rig/Control/Base.  SymWing also has an unrelated
    Control/Flight01/Base.

    charrig.usda references /FeathersRig at /CharRig/Rig and relocates both
    Rig/RWing/Control -> Control/RWing and the nested
    Rig/RWing/Deform/Flight01Rig/Control -> Control/RWing/Flight01.  So
    /CharRig/Control/RWing/Flight01 is the target of the nested relocate,
    which elides the ancestral opinions from Rig/RWing/Control/Flight01 (and
    from the SymWing class there).  charrig.usda also authors an opinion on
    /CharRig/Rig/SymWing/Control/Flight01/Base.

    root.usda just references /CharRig at /Saverio.  We expect
    /Saverio/Control/RWing/Flight01/X to compose the same opinions as
    /CharRig/Control/RWing/Flight01/X does in charrig.usda alone: the
    RWing/Deform and SymWing/Deform opinions on Base, and none from
    SymWing/Control/Flight01/Base, which the nested relocate elides.
    Previously, the elided class was implied into root.usda, where it
    contributed opinions.
    """
)

def "Saverio" (
    references = @./charrig.usda@</CharRig>
)
{
}
